================================================================================
TERMS
================================================================================

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

   a) Use this mod in your own RimWorld games, alone or in any modlist.

   b) Read the source code, learn from it, and discuss it publicly.

   c) Modify your own local copy for your own private use.

   d) Create content with the in-game editor that this mod provides, such as
      pieces, settlements, object lists, loot tables and pawn lists. That
      content is yours. You may publish and license it as you see fit, and it
      is not covered by this license even though it needs this mod to run.

   e) Report bugs, suggest changes, and submit patches.


2. WHAT NEEDS MY PERMISSION FIRST

   Everything that leaves your own machine:

   a) Publishing a modified version of this mod, in whole or in part, anywhere.
      This includes the Steam Workshop, GitHub, Discord, Nexus, modpacks, and
      any other distribution channel.

   b) Redistributing this mod, modified or not, outside the channels I publish
      it on myself.

   c) Including this mod, or parts of its code or assets, in another mod or in
      any other software.

   d) Using the code or assets of this mod commercially.

   Ask first. I am easy to reach and I usually say yes. Open an issue in the
   repository, write me on Steam, or use any other channel where you know me.


3. IF THIS MOD IS ABANDONED

   If I am unreachable for twelve consecutive months and the mod is broken on
   the current RimWorld version, anyone may publish a fixed version, provided
   they credit me, link to the original, and take the version down at my
   request if I return.

   This exists so the mod does not die with me being busy. It is not a way to
   take it over while I am still around.


4. THIRD PARTY CONTENT

   This mod reads definitions and textures from other mods at runtime through
   their published names and paths. Those assets remain the property of their
   respective authors and are not covered by this license. Nothing from other
   mods is copied into this repository or patched by it.

   Harmony is referenced as a dependency and is licensed separately by its
   author.


5. NO WARRANTY

   This mod is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied. The author is not liable for any damage arising from its use,
   including but not limited to corrupted saves.


6. STEAM WORKSHOP

   Uploading to the Steam Workshop grants Valve rights under the Steam
   Subscriber Agreement. Those rights exist independently of this license and
   are not affected by it.


